## Context

Second tranche (tracker 0550): the conductor exists and runs only the
tick. N × P0 elect exactly one conductor through the lease row; the
pipeline does not multiply with N.

## Relevant files

- SPEC.md §5.2.5: lease UPDATE idiom, UUID holder, TTL 20 s = 2 ×
  heartbeat, election check 10 s, migration gate < 30 s; the CAS
  commit-guard idiom; orphan rules (stdin EOF, holder re-check between
  micro-batches).

## Actions

1. Lease acquisition/renewal on the injected clock; renewal decoupled
   from stage progress.
2. Election check in every P0; the winner runs the tick from tranche 1.
3. Orphan repairs: exit on stdin EOF; holder re-verification hook (used
   from tranche 3 on).

## Test

- Red first: two P0 processes on one data directory — exactly one
  conductor; kill -9 it twice, another takes over within TTL + cadence
  (virtual time), per the SPEC soak clause.

## Verification

- [ ] Deposed-but-running conductor's conditional UPDATE writes nothing
- [ ] Failover duplicate work bounded per SPEC's honest R13 restatement

## Invariants

- Query path stays write-free; upstream tests green.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Election + lease merged on a fork branch, soak test green
